<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Full proofs</h2>

<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Proposition 2.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\left(K^{\top}V\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\left(K^{\top}V\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is shift-invariant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">The problem can be simplified by considering an arbitrary entry in <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\top}V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\top}V</annotation></semantics></math>, since</span></p>
<table id="A1.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(K^{\top}V\right)_{i,j}=K_{i}^{\top}V_{j}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(K^{\top}V\right)_{i,j}=K_{i}^{\top}V_{j}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i},\,V_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i},\,V_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>j</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j</annotation></semantics></math>-th columns of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>, representing 1-dimensional signals.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Parseval theorem, this inner product between signals equals to their inner product in Fourier domain:</span></p>
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{i}^{\top}V_{j}=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}}\left(\omega\right)\hat{V_{j}}^{*}\left(\omega\right)d\omega\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{i}^{\top}V_{j}=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}}\left(\omega\right)\hat{V_{j}}^{*}\left(\omega\right)d\omega\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> the queries and values of a <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-shifted input signal w.r.t. the input signal of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.
Following <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1. ‣ Shift-Equivariant Attention. ‣ 2.3 Alias-Free Vision Transformer ‣ 2 Methods ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, a translation by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> of the input <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> yields a translation by <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> of both <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Fourier transform of the translated signals differs by a phase which cancels out in the inner product, thus we get the same product:</span></p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle K_{i}^{\tau\top}V_{j}^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em">⊤</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle K_{i}^{\tau\top}V_{j}^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}^{\tau}}\left(\omega\right)\hat{V_{j}^{\tau}}^{*}\left(\omega\right)d\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>τ</mi></msubsup><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}^{\tau}}\left(\omega\right)\hat{V_{j}^{\tau}}^{*}\left(\omega\right)d\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}}\left(\omega\right)e^{j\omega\tau}\left(\hat{V_{j}}\left(\omega\right)e^{j\omega\tau}\right)^{*}d\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}}\left(\omega\right)e^{j\omega\tau}\left(\hat{V_{j}}\left(\omega\right)e^{j\omega\tau}\right)^{*}d\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}}\left(\omega\right)\hat{V_{j}}^{*}\left(\omega\right)d\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mi>π</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{2\pi}\int_{-\pi}^{\pi}\hat{K_{i}}\left(\omega\right)\hat{V_{j}}^{*}\left(\omega\right)d\omega</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=K_{i}^{\top}V_{j}\&gt;." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=K_{i}^{\top}V_{j}\&gt;.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Class Attention.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we formalize the statement regarding shift-invariance of the Class Attention layer in <a href="#S2.SS3" title="2.3 Alias-Free Vision Transformer ‣ 2 Methods ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 4</span></span><span id="Thmproposition4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q=XW_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>q</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q=XW_{q}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=XW_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=XW_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V=XW_{v}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>v</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V=XW_{v}</annotation></semantics></math> be the query, key and value matrices of a patch sequence <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Append the sequence with a class token,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Q}\;=\;\left[Q^{\top},\,q_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\qquad\tilde{K}\;=\;\left[K^{\top},\,k_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\qquad\tilde{V}\;=\;\left[V^{\top},\,v_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Q}\;=\;\left[Q^{\top},\,q_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\qquad\tilde{K}\;=\;\left[K^{\top},\,k_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\qquad\tilde{V}\;=\;\left[V^{\top},\,v_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">with learnable vectors <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{cls}},k_{\mathrm{cls}},v_{\mathrm{cls}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{cls}},k_{\mathrm{cls}},v_{\mathrm{cls}}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Our CA layer applies the SEA update</span></p>
<table id="A1.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}^{\prime}\;=\;\mathrm{SEA}\!\left(\tilde{Q},\,\tilde{K},\,\tilde{V}\right)\;=\;\tilde{Q}\,f\!\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{\left(N+1\right)\times D}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:2.047em;" width="2.047em"><mi>SEA</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.427em;" width="0.427em"><mi>f</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo rspace="0.280em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{\prime}\;=\;\mathrm{SEA}\!\left(\tilde{Q},\,\tilde{K},\,\tilde{V}\right)\;=\;\tilde{Q}\,f\!\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)\;\in\;\mathbb{R}^{\left(N+1\right)\times D},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmproposition4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where
<math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\colon\mathbb{R}^{\left(D\times D\right)}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\colon\mathbb{R}^{\left(D\times D\right)}\!\to\!\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>
is any matrix function.
Denote the output by
<math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}^{\prime}=\left[V^{\prime\,\top},\,v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\prime}\right]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo>′</mo><mo lspace="0.392em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{\prime}=\left[V^{\prime\,\top},\,v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\prime}\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
with <math id="Thmproposition4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}^{N\times D}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then</span></p>
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Patch equivariance:</span><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
</span><math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is shift-equivariant.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Class invariance:</span><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">
</span><math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is shift-invariant.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> be the keys and values obtained from the <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>-translated input <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>, and define</span></p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Q}^{\tau}\;=\;\left[\left(Q^{\tau}\right)^{\top},\,q_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\quad\tilde{K}^{\tau}\;=\;\left[\left(K^{\tau}\right)^{\top},\,k_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\quad\tilde{V}^{\tau}\;=\;\left[\left(V^{\tau}\right)^{\top},\,v_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>Q</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Q}^{\tau}\;=\;\left[\left(Q^{\tau}\right)^{\top},\,q_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\quad\tilde{K}^{\tau}\;=\;\left[\left(K^{\tau}\right)^{\top},\,k_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top},\quad\tilde{V}^{\tau}\;=\;\left[\left(V^{\tau}\right)^{\top},\,v_{\mathrm{cls}}\right]^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Shift-invariance of the attention weights.</span>
Since the translation <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> acts only on patch tokens, we get</p>
<table id="A1.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{K}^{\tau\,\top}\tilde{V}^{\tau}\;=\;\left(K^{\tau}\right)^{\!\top}V^{\tau}+k_{\mathrm{cls}}v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}\;=\;K^{\top}V+k_{\mathrm{cls}}v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}\;=\;\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0.392em">⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mi>τ</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>K</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{K}^{\tau\,\top}\tilde{V}^{\tau}\;=\;\left(K^{\tau}\right)^{\!\top}V^{\tau}+k_{\mathrm{cls}}v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}\;=\;K^{\top}V+k_{\mathrm{cls}}v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}\;=\;\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where the middle equality uses <a href="#Thmproposition2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ Shift-Equivariant Attention. ‣ 2.3 Alias-Free Vision Transformer ‣ 2 Methods ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.
The rank-one class term <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{\mathrm{cls}}v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>cls</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>cls</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{\mathrm{cls}}v_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is constant (independent of the input translation), hence <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V})</annotation></semantics></math> is shift-invariant.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">It holds that</span></p>
<table id="A1.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{V}^{\prime}=\tilde{Q}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)=\left[Q^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right),\,q_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)\right]^{\top}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Q</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>cls</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{V}^{\prime}=\tilde{Q}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)=\left[Q^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right),\,q_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)\right]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Patch equivariance.</span>
From <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ Class Attention. ‣ Appendix A Full proofs ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>, the patch tokens post CA are <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\prime}=Q^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Q</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\prime}=Q^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)</annotation></semantics></math> is shift-invariant, therefore <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> is shift-equivariant similar to <a href="#Thmproposition3" title="Proposition 3. ‣ Shift-Equivariant Attention. ‣ 2.3 Alias-Free Vision Transformer ‣ 2 Methods ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Class invariance.</span>
From <a href="#A1.E19" title="In Proof. ‣ Class Attention. ‣ Appendix A Full proofs ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>, the class token post CA is <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>cls</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>K</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>V</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\mathrm{cls}}^{\top}f\left(\tilde{K}^{\top}\tilde{V}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is shift-invariant.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Additional results</h2>

<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Additional datasets</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate all models from <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Accuracy and shift consistency ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> on three additional classification benchmarks — CIFAR-10, CIFAR-100 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">36</a>]</cite>, and Stanford Cars <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib35" title="" class="ltx_ref">35</a>]</cite> — under two protocols: (i) fine-tuning ImageNet-pretrained checkpoints and (ii) training from scratch.
In both protocols, we train each model using the ImageNet recipe of <a href="#A4.T8" title="In Appendix D Experiments details ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> with <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1{,}000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1,000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1{,}000</annotation></semantics></math> epochs, where in the fine-tuning protocol, we initialize the model weights using the checkpoints from <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Accuracy and shift consistency ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.
We report top-1 accuracy together with cyclic shift consistency for integer and half-pixel translations, defined exactly as in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Accuracy and shift consistency ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Across all datasets, AFT maintains near-perfect shift-equivariance (above 99% consistency in integer and half-pixel shifts).
Additionally, when fine-tuned, the XCiT-Small-AF model is slightly but consistently more accurate than the baseline on all three datasets, suggesting that the shift-invariance prior can benefit larger transformers when adapting to small datasets.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 4</span>: </span><span id="A2.T4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">CIFAR and Stanford Cars (fine-tuning): accuracy and cyclic shift consistency.<span id="A2.T4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> We fine-tune ImageNet-pretrained checkpoints on CIFAR-10/100 and Stanford Cars. Metrics are top-1 test accuracy and consistency to integer and half-pixel cyclic translations (as in <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Accuracy and shift consistency ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Alias-Free ViT: Fractional Shift Invariance via Linear Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>).</span></span></figcaption>
<div id="A2.T4.6" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:56.1pt;vertical-align:-26.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-165.6pt,26.9pt) scale(0.510196105544942,0.510196105544942) ;">
